            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>When to Use This SOP</h2>
<p>This guide applies when your team manages multiple overseas advertising platforms (Meta, Google, TikTok, etc.) with monthly budgets exceeding $100,000 USD. Manual tracking of account balances and recharge timing becomes impractical at this scale. The following SOP is designed for mid-to-large sized出海 teams with dedicated operations or finance reconciliation staff.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Build a Complete Account Asset Inventory</h2>
<p><strong>Key Actions:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Export account lists from all advertising platforms, including Account ID, account owner, current balance, and billing method (prepay vs. monthly invoicing)</li>
<li>Calculate "days until depletion" based on each account's average daily spend</li>
<li>Categorize accounts by platform and campaign objective</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Decision Rule:</strong> If Average Daily Spend × 3 &gt; Current Balance → Add to high-priority monitoring list</p>
</blockquote>
<p>One app team's finance team discovered they had overpaid approximately $8,000 USD because monthly invoicing credit limits were not clearly marked. After completing this step, all accounts should be visible in a single spreadsheet for unified monitoring.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Configure Multi-Tier Balance Alert Rules</h2>
<p><strong>Three alert levels:</strong></p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Alert Level</th>
<th>Trigger Condition</th>
<th>Response Timeframe</th>
<th>Responsible Party</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Yellow Alert</td>
<td>Balance covers 5-7 days of spend</td>
<td>Within 24 hours</td>
<td>Campaign Operations</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Orange Alert</td>
<td>Balance covers 2-4 days of spend</td>
<td>Within 4 hours</td>
<td>Operations + Finance</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Red Alert</td>
<td>Balance covers less than 2 days</td>
<td>Immediate response</td>
<td>Finance leads recharge</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Configuration Methods:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Meta Business Manager</strong>: Enable "Account Spending Limit" notifications in ad account settings</li>
<li><strong>Google Ads</strong>: Use scripts or third-party tools (Sprout Social, Optmyzr) to set balance alerts</li>
<li><strong>TikTok Ads</strong>: Native balance alerts are unavailable; integrate via API with your own monitoring system</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> Recharge processing times vary significantly across platforms. Meta prepay accounts typically credit instantly, while monthly invoicing accounts require additional attention to billing cycles.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Establish Recharge Approval Workflow</h2>
<p><strong>Standard Process (amounts ≥ $5,000 USD):</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Operations submits recharge request with account details, amount, and justification</li>
<li>Finance verifies account ownership and budget approval records</li>
<li>Treasury executes the recharge and preserves payment receipts</li>
<li>Operations confirms balance credit and notifies team via email/chat</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Approval SLA:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>During business hours: Orange Alert approvals within 30 minutes</li>
<li>Outside business hours: Finance maintains an emergency recharge channel with on-call staff authorized to handle Red Alerts directly</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Conduct Weekly Financial Reconciliation</h2>
<p><strong>Reconciliation Checklist:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Platform-reported spend vs. recharge records</li>
<li>Check for abnormal charges (accidental clicks, unclosed historical campaigns)</li>
<li>Verify rebate and coupon deductions are correctly applied</li>
<li>Confirm account balances match billing period (monthly invoice amounts should align)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Deliverable:</strong> Reconciliation report (by platform) + variance explanation (if any)</p>
<p>One跨境电商 team discovered a 3% discrepancy between TikTok spend and recharges due to delayed billing. Weekly reconciliation ensured such issues were identified and resolved within 7 days.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 5: Establish Monthly Fund Review Mechanism</h2>
<p><strong>Review Dimensions:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Fund Utilization Rate</strong>: Actual spend ÷ Total recharge amount; below 95% requires investigation</li>
<li><strong>Alert Response Time</strong>: Distribution of time from alert trigger to recharge completion</li>
<li><strong>Recharge Frequency</strong>: If a single account requires more than 4 recharges per month, budget allocation needs optimization</li>
<li><strong>Exchange Rate Loss</strong>: Evaluation of currency conversion costs for multi-currency recharges</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Optimization Actions:</strong> Based on review findings, adjust budget allocation ratios across accounts to reduce small, frequent recharges and minimize fees and exchange rate losses.</p>
<hr />
<h2>FAQ</h2>
<p><strong>Q: How to reallocate funds when account balances are uneven?</strong></p>
<p>Prioritize shifting budget from low-spend accounts to high-spend accounts rather than making direct recharges. Cross-entity transfers require confirmation that platform policies allow such transfers.</p>
<p><strong>Q: What happens if I forget to pay a monthly invoice?</strong></p>
<p>Most platforms will suspend ad delivery and charge late fees. Set calendar reminders on the invoice date each month, with Finance confirming payment.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Execution Checklist</h2>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Complete asset inventory for all accounts</li>
<li>[ ] Three-tier alert rules configured and tested</li>
<li>[ ] Recharge approval process documented and communicated</li>
<li>[ ] Weekly reconciliation responsible party assigned</li>
<li>[ ] Monthly review mechanism scheduled</li>
</ul>
<p>By following these 5 steps, your team can shift overseas ad spend management from reactive to proactive control, preventing funding issues from impacting campaign performance.</p>
